jobs.description:
SamenvattingDo you see a challenge in loading, unloading and carefully checking freight? Do you want to work in a dynamic, international environment? Become a Warehouse Mail Employee at Schiphol-Rijk, full-time! Good work!Over de functieAs a Warehouse Post employee, you will play an important role in loading and unloading goods and work closely with your team in a dynamic environment. Flexibility, cooperation and customer orientation are key. What will you do?
- Mail acceptance and processing;
- Sorting mail bags and parcels;
- Performing light administrative tasks;
- ULD assembly and disassembly;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Transport on the platform

You will work in a diverse team and follow a schedule with three different shifts:
- Morning shift: 07:00 - 15:30 
- Afternoon shift: 15:00 - 23:30 
- Night shift: 23:00 - 07:00 

Over het bedrijfAt this leading company, you will have the opportunity to work in a dynamic environment where teamwork and efficiency are key. As a leading player in the logistics sector, the organization offers a challenging work environment where you can further develop your skills and play an important role in the efficient handling of shipments.
Wat wij vragen- Have logistics experience;
- Willing to follow internal courses;
- Good Command of the Dutch or/and English language;
- Ready to work physically;
- You can obtain a Certificate of No Objection (VGB) ( which we will apply for) meaning you should have at least 8 years of registration within the EU.

These points are very important to start working as a Warehouse Post Employee at Schiphol-Rijk. We are also curious about who you are. Curious about your talents, background and ideas. Surprise us.
Wat wij bieden- € 16.70  € 16,99 gross salary per hour, depending on relevant work experience (including 2,5% year-end bonus) 
- Supplements for evening, night weekend shifts and public holidays, ranging from 125% to 140%
- Holiday allowances of 200%
- Weekly payments with 8.33% vac

SamenvattingStart as an Orderpicker in Woerden and help keep Jumbo stores stocked across the Netherlands. Earn up to €23.39 gross per hour, and enjoy a hands-on logistics job with clear routines and a supportive team. No specific education required, just motivation and a willingness to learn. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker, you’ll prepare orders for Jumbo stores across the Netherlands using a modern voice-pick system. Depending on the assignment, you will work in a warm (+18°C) or chilled (+2°C to +4°C) area at the warehouse.

Your tasks:
-  Picking orders with a voice-pick system;
-  Placing products on trolleys or pallets;
-  Checking orders for accuracy and quality;
-  Keeping your workspace clean and organized;
-  Following warehouse and safety procedures;

This job is for 32–40 hours per week in a two-shift system, with occasional weekend work.
The worktimes are from 06.00 - 14:00 and 14.00 - 21:00.
Over het bedrijfAt Jumbo’s distribution centre in Woerden, teamwork keeps things moving. Every day, colleagues work together to prepare orders and make sure stores across the Netherlands receive the groceries and everyday products their customers need. You will join a modern, well-organized workplace where everyone plays a part. Clear procedures, a focus on quality and helpful colleagues make it a great place to gain experience in logistics and develop your skills.
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- Basic English skills to understand instructions and communicate with your team
- Willingness to work in warm and chilled areas;
- Physically stable and comfortable with walking and lifting during the shift;
- You are available to work in 2-shifts.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.
Wat wij bieden- A salary between €14.99 and €15.21 gross per hour for work in the warm warehouse and €15.37–€15.59
